      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T10:53:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is listNoneIpmiGroupUsers intentionally only an in-memory cache? What is the expected recovery behavior after restart or crash? Should the list always be rebuilt from D-Bus, or should it be persisted?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 519,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 519,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "6d636392699443a4e24b02ab845837de6c6d4b68",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13488af1_a3af4d9b",
        "filename": "user_channel/user_mgmt.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 519,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002977
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T05:46:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is intentionally in-memory only. phosphor-user-manager is the source of truth for group membership, so persisting a copy here would duplicate state that can drift; the list is always rebuilt from D-Bus, never persisted.\n\nRecovery: on every ipmid start, cacheUserDataFile() rebuilds it from user-manager with GetManagedObjects (around line 1640). At runtime the InterfacesAdded/InterfacesRemoved, UserRenamed and PropertiesChanged(UserGroups) handlers keep it in sync. After a restart or crash the constructor runs again, so the list is recovered the same way. If it were ever out of date, user-manager still enforces the limit.",
      "parentUuid": "5031a793_ab4d972b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 519,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 519,
        "endChar": 27
      },
